/*
:name: type_boolean
:type: error
:error: `boolean` was renamed `Bool`
*/

// User rulings 2026-09-28 (37) and 2026-09-29 (52): the boolean type is `Bool`
// (and `Bool(x)` the cast). The old lowercase spellings (`bool`, `boolean`) are
// banned words, so `:boolean` is a clear error that names the new spelling
// (before ruling 52 it pointed at `:bool`; before ruling 37 it was the generic
// "`boolean` is not a type" with a hint to declare a type named `boolean`).
pub mod type_boolean(a:boolean) -> (o:Bool@[0]) {  // locate_error_here
  o = a
}
